ch promotes scientific renewal, pursues scientific breakthroughs and seeks solutions for the benefit of society.\nAcademy Professor applications are invited from individual researchers who are already at the international forefront of their fields and who can become top international researchers during their terms. Successful candidates will be expected to demonstrate a wide range of impact both during and after the funding period. They shall also present a concrete plan for continuing internationally high-quality research beyond the funding period.\nThe six-year funding can cover the applicant’s salary, the salary costs of a possible research team and other research costs.\nBackground and objectives\nAt the core of the Research Council of Finland’s activities is to provide funding for excellent scientific research. The research we fund is also expected to have high scientific and societal\nimpact\nand follow the principles of\nresponsible science\n.\nA post as Academy Professor is intended for high-calibre scientists whose research promotes scientific renewal, pursues scientific breakthroughs and seeks solutions for the benefit of society.\nThe aim of the Academy Professorship funding is that the applicant, who is already at the international forefront of their field, not only becomes a top international researcher during the term, but is also able to strengthen and raise the level of expertise in the field in Finland.\nThe funding is granted for up to six years. Funding can be granted for the researcher’s own salary and other costs associated with the implementation of the research plan.\nPrint page\nSpark – Novel and bold research ideas with long-term focus\nThe aim of the RCF funding category Spark is to ensure a high-quality scientific foundation for the Finnish research and innovation system now and in the future.\nSpark funding identifies researcher-driven bold research ideas and advances innovative, broad-based research in the long term.\nShare page\nSpark –