    "objective": "Anticipatory call for proposals for research teams — Adolescents Thrive: African Adolescents Bolstered through Local Evidence (AABLE) | IDRC - International Development Research Centre\nSkip to main content\nTo homepage\nTo homepage\nEnglish\nFrançais\nEspañol\nToggle Menu\nToggle Menu\nFulltext search\nMobile Main Navigation\nWhat we do\nWhere we work\nHow we work\nProjects we support\nClimate resilient food systems\nGlobal health\nEducation and science\nDemocratic and inclusive governance\nSustainable inclusive economies\nFunding\nGrants and awards\nApplying for funding\nManaging funds\nResources for IDRC grantees\n",
    "description": "Anticipatory call for proposals for research teams — Adolescents Thrive: African Adolescents Bolstered through Local Evidence (AABLE) | IDRC - International Development Research Centre\nSkip to main content\nTo homepage\nTo homepage\nEnglish\nFrançais\nEspañol\nToggle Menu\nToggle Menu\nFulltext search\nMobile Main Navigation\nWhat we do\nWhere we work\nHow we work\nProjects we support\nClimate resilient food systems\nGlobal health\nEducation and science\nDemocratic and inclusive governance\nSustainable inclusive economies\nFunding\nGrants and awards\nApplying for funding\nManaging funds\nResources for IDRC grantees\nPartnerships\nAbout IDRC\nAbout\nCareers\nAnnual review\nTransparency\nLeadership\nPolicies and commitments\nNews and events\nNews\nEvents\nPerspectives\nResearch in Action\nStories\nMedia\nTo homepage\nEnglish\nFrançais\nEspañol\nToggle Menu\nFooter\nCareers\nContact Us\nDigital library\nSub Footer Menu\nAccessibility\nEquality Statement\nOpen access policy\nPrivacy Notice\nResearch ethics\nTerms of use\nTransparency\nMain navigation\nWhat we do\nWhere we work\nHow we work\nProjects we support\nClimate resilient food systems\nGlobal health\nEducation and science\nDemocratic and inclusive governance\nSustainable inclusive economies\nFunding\nGrants and awards\nApplying for funding\nManaging funds\nResources for IDRC grantees\nPartnerships\nAbout IDRC\nAbout\nCareers\nAnnual review\nTransparency\nLeadership\nPolicies and commitments\nNews and events\nNews\nEvents\nPerspectives\nResearch in Action\nStories\nMedia\nFulltext search\nHome\nFunding\nAnticipatory call for proposals for research teams — Adolescents Thrive: African Adolescents Bolstered through Local Evidence (AABLE)\nClosed\nCall for\nProposals\nDeadline\nThursday, August 7, 2025 - 10:00 ET\nPrograms\nGlobal Health\nDuration\nUp to 30 months\nFunded by\nIDRC\nBudget\nCAD 692 000\nPoint of contact\nAABLE@idrc.ca\nType\nGrant\nStatus\nClosed\nScope\nThis call for proposals will support implementation research that addresses challenges in adolescent sexual and reproductive health in 13 African countries: Côte d’Ivoire, Ethiopia, Ghana, Kenya, Liberia, Malawi, Mozambique, Nigeria, Senegal, Sierra Leone, Tanzania, Zambia, and Zimbabwe.\nProjects must align with one of the following four priority themes:\nTheme 1: Service Delivery Models\nTheme 2: Social, Economic, or Multisectoral Policy Interventions\nTheme 3: Data and Health Management Information Systems (HMIS)\nTheme 4: Digital Health Technologies\nUp to eight grants, each with a maximum value of CAD692,000 will be awarded for a period of up to 30 months, including all research activities and the submission of the final report. Selected projects are anticipated to begin on November 1, 2025.\nEligibility\nResearch teams from the selected African countries, working on adolescent sexual and reproductive health and rights. The teams need to meet the eligibility criteria outlined in the call.\nMore details\nFor more information, please consult the detailed\nCall for Proposals\nand the\nFrequently Asked Questions\n.\nIf you have any questions about this call, please contact the AABLE team at\nAABLE@idrc.ca\nbefore July 31, 2025 at 11:59 p.m. EDT.\nFollowing the launch of the call for proposals, IDRC will organize an information session to address any queries from potential applicants. This will take place on July 3, 2025, from 8:00 to 9:00 a.m. EDT. Click\nhere\nto join the session.\nReady to apply?\nTo apply for this funding opportunity, you’ll need an account on SurveyMonkey Apply. If you don’t have an account yet, or need help with your existing one, please refer to our\nAccount setup guide\n.\nGet started\nShare this page\nStay connected.\nSubscribe\nIDRC / Eduardo Jalil, Panos Pictures\nFooter\nCareers\nContact Us\nDigital library\nMedia\nSub Footer Menu\nAccessibility\nEquality Statement\nOpen access policy\nPrivacy Notice\nResearch ethics\nTerms of use\nTransparency\n©\t2026\nIDRC",
