    "objective": "Call for letters of interest: Addressing neglected areas of sexual and reproductive health and rights in sub-Saharan Africa (ANeSA) | IDRC - International Development Research Centre\nSkip to main content\nTo homepage\nTo homepage\nEnglish\nFrançais\nEspañol\nToggle Menu\nToggle Menu\nFulltext search\nMobile Main Navigation\nWhat we do\nWhere we work\nHow we work\nProjects we support\nClimate resilient food systems\nGlobal health\nEducation and science\nDemocratic and inclusive governance\nSustainable inclusive economies\nFunding\nGrants and awards\nApplying for funding\nManaging funds\nResources for IDRC grantees\nPa",
    "description": "Call for letters of interest: Addressing neglected areas of sexual and reproductive health and rights in sub-Saharan Africa (ANeSA) | IDRC - International Development Research Centre\nSkip to main content\nTo homepage\nTo homepage\nEnglish\nFrançais\nEspañol\nToggle Menu\nToggle Menu\nFulltext search\nMobile Main Navigation\nWhat we do\nWhere we work\nHow we work\nProjects we support\nClimate resilient food systems\nGlobal health\nEducation and science\nDemocratic and inclusive governance\nSustainable inclusive economies\nFunding\nGrants and awards\nApplying for funding\nManaging funds\nResources for IDRC grantees\nPartnerships\nAbout IDRC\nAbout\nCareers\nAnnual review\nTransparency\nLeadership\nPolicies and commitments\nNews and events\nNews\nEvents\nPerspectives\nResearch in Action\nStories\nMedia\nTo homepage\nEnglish\nFrançais\nEspañol\nToggle Menu\nFooter\nCareers\nContact Us\nDigital library\nSub Footer Menu\nAccessibility\nEquality Statement\nOpen access policy\nPrivacy Notice\nResearch ethics\nTerms of use\nTransparency\nMain navigation\nWhat we do\nWhere we work\nHow we work\nProjects we support\nClimate resilient food systems\nGlobal health\nEducation and science\nDemocratic and inclusive governance\nSustainable inclusive economies\nFunding\nGrants and awards\nApplying for funding\nManaging funds\nResources for IDRC grantees\nPartnerships\nAbout IDRC\nAbout\nCareers\nAnnual review\nTransparency\nLeadership\nPolicies and commitments\nNews and events\nNews\nEvents\nPerspectives\nResearch in Action\nStories\nMedia\nFulltext search\nHome\nFunding\nCall for letters of interest: Addressing neglected areas of sexual and reproductive health and rights in sub-Saharan Africa (ANeSA)\nClosed\nCall for\nLetters of interest\nDeadline\nSunday, August 23, 2026 - 23:59 ET\nPrograms\nGlobal Health\nDuration\nUp to 36 months\nFunded by\nInternational Development Research Centre (IDRC), Global Affairs Canada (GAC), and the Canadian Institutes of Health Research (CIHR)\nBudget\nUp to six grants of up to CAD 1.2 million each. Up to 12 applicants will be invited to submit a Full Proposal.\nPoint of contact\nSRHR-SDSR@idrc.ca\nType\nGrant\nStatus\nClosed\nScope\nAddressing Neglected Areas of Sexual and Reproductive Health and Rights in sub-Saharan Africa (ANeSA) is launching Stage 1 of a two-stage funding opportunity to support Cohort 2 of Implementation Research Teams. The initiative will fund implementation research focused on sustainable, evidence-informed and gender-transformative interventions that address neglected areas of sexual and reproductive health and rights for under-served populations in sub-Saharan Africa. Up to six grants of up to CAD 1.2 million each will be awarded, and up to 12 applicants will be invited to advance to the Full Proposal stage.\nSuccessful projects will address at least one of ANeSA’s five priority areas:\nImproving access to family planning and contraceptive services\nExpanding access to safe abortion care, where legally permitted, and post-abortion care (APAC)\nUpholding SRHR rights and ensuring access to services for adolescents\nPreventing sexual- and gender-based violence (SGBV) and improving services for people experiencing SGBV\nStrengthening advocacy for SRHR\nFor more information, please consult the\nCall for Letters of Interest.\nEligibility\nThis call is open to Implementation Research Teams led by a sub-Saharan Africa-based researcher affiliated with an eligible institution in an eligible country. Please refer to the Call for Letters of Interest for the full team composition and eligibility requirements.\nMore details\nLearn more about\nANeSA\n.\nFor more information, please consult the\nFrequently Asked Questions (FAQ) page\n.\nPlease note that this page will be updated regularly. This version is current as of July 20, 2026.\nMore questions? Please contact the ANeSA team at SRHR-SDSR@idrc.ca by August 09, 2026, to receive a response before the submission deadline.\nThe informational webinars held on\nJuly 15 and 16, 2026 both reached maximum capacity\n. Due to the high level of interest in this call for proposals and sinc",
