    "objective": "At the core of the Research Council of Finland’s activities is to provide funding for excellent scientific research. The research we fund is also expected to have high scientific and societal impact and follow the principles of responsible science",
    "description": "Clinical Researcher Fundi - Research Council of Finland\nTo main content\nAbout the RCF\nAbout us\nRCF at a glance\nStrategy\nSustainable development\nAcademicians of Science\nRCF Awards\nWorking at the RCF\nContact us\nRCF organisation\nOrganisation\nManagement\nDecision-making bodies\nWhat's new\nPress releases and news\nOpinions\nNewsletter\nBlog\nEvents\nMedia services\nResearch funding\nFunding opportunities\nSpark funding\nAcademy Project Funding\nAcademy Research Fellowship\nAcademy Professorship\nClinical Researcher Funding\nForge funding\nFinnish Flagships\nResearch infrastructures\nFinnish Centres of Excellence\nInternational collaboration in high-performance computing\nShift funding\nProof of Concept Funding\nFunding for clinical research\nFunding for university research profiles\nInternational funding cooperation\nFunding from EU Recovery and Resilience Facility (RRF)\nSport Science and Physical Activity – ACTIVE\nStrategic research funding\nApply for funding\nCalls for applications\nA–Z index of application guidelines\nAsk & Apply\nHow to use funding\nReport on your project\nReview and funding decisions\nHow applications are reviewed\nReview and decision-making\nGuidelines and forms for reviewers\nHow decisions are made\nFunding decisions\nResponsible Science\nFrom research to society\nResearch impact\nNew knowledge\nExpertise and experts\nInnovations for business and society\nRCF impact\nData dashboards\nPublications\nInternational cooperation\nOpinions\nEvents\nResponsible science\nResponsible research funding\nGood scientific practice and research ethics\nResearch security\nEquality and nondiscrimination\nOpen science\nSustainable development\nResponsible researcher evaluation\nOnline services\nFI\nSV\nFI\nSV\nOnline services\nResearch Council of Finland\nResearch funding\nFunding opportunities\nSpark funding\nClinical Researcher Funding\nClinical Researcher Funding\nThe Research Council of Finland funds part-time research by physicians and researchers engaged in clinical practice.\nThe call for applications for Clinical Researcher Funding will not be opened in 2025–2026.\nThe Research Council of Finland funds part-time research by physicians and researchers engaged in clinical practice. The aim is to promote clinical research careers in cooperation with, for example, university hospitals, and to encourage medical doctors and other researchers working in clinical practice to engage in research.\nThose eligible to apply are medical doctors with a doctoral degree (DMedSc, DDS or DVM) working in clinical practice or other healthcare professionals with a doctoral degree engaged in clinical practice. Funding will not be granted to professors or full-time university researchers (\ncareer stages I–IV\n).\nBackground and objectives\nAt the core of the Research Council of Finland’s activities is to provide funding for excellent scientific research. The research we fund is also expected to have high scientific and societal\nimpact\nand follow the principles of\nresponsible science\n.\nWe fund part-time research by physicians and researchers engaged in clinical practice. The aim is to promote clinical research careers in cooperation with, for example, university hospitals, and to encourage medical doctors and other researchers working in clinical practice to engage in research.\nPrint page\nSpark – Novel and bold research ideas with long-term focus\nThe aim of the RCF funding category Spark is to ensure a high-quality scientific foundation for the Finnish research and innovation system now and in the future.\nSpark funding identifies researcher-driven bold research ideas and advances innovative, broad-based research in the long term.\nShare page\nSpark – Novel and bold research ideas with long-term focus\nThe aim of the RCF funding category Spark is to ensure a high-quality scientific foundation for the Finnish research and innovation system now and in the future.\nSpark funding identifies researcher-driven bold research ideas and advances innovative, broad-based research in the long term.\nShare page\nDo you have questions or ",
