  {
    "id": "idrc-international-development-research-centre-d6a9e0a65e28",
    "entity_id": "idrc-international-development-research-centre",
    "entity_name": "IDRC – International Development Research Centre",
    "title": "Connecting Indigenous Research Leadership in Canada and the Global South",
    "link": "https://idrc-crdi.ca/en/funding/connecting-indigenous-research-leadership-canada-and-global-south",
    "objective": "to co-develop an interdisciplinary, Indigenous research agenda and build alliances between Indigenous researchers in the Global South and First Nations, Métis and Inuit researchers in Canada, potentially leading to broader joint research endeavors in the future",
    "description": "Connecting Indigenous Research Leadership in Canada and the Global South | IDRC - International Development Research Centre\nSkip to main content\nTo homepage\nTo homepage\nEnglish\nFrançais\nEspañol\nToggle Menu\nToggle Menu\nFulltext search\nMobile Main Navigation\nWhat we do\nWhere we work\nHow we work\nProjects we support\nClimate resilient food systems\nGlobal health\nEducation and science\nDemocratic and inclusive governance\nSustainable inclusive economies\nFunding\nGrants and awards\nApplying for funding\nManaging funds\nResources for IDRC grantees\nPartnerships\nAbout IDRC\nAbout\nCareers\nAnnual review\nTransparency\nLeadership\nPolicies and commitments\nNews and events\nNews\nEvents\nPerspectives\nResearch in Action\nStories\nMedia\nTo homepage\nEnglish\nFrançais\nEspañol\nToggle Menu\nFooter\nCareers\nContact Us\nDigital library\nSub Footer Menu\nAccessibility\nEquality Statement\nOpen access policy\nPrivacy Notice\nResearch ethics\nTerms of use\nTransparency\nMain navigation\nWhat we do\nWhere we work\nHow we work\nProjects we support\nClimate resilient food systems\nGlobal health\nEducation and science\nDemocratic and inclusive governance\nSustainable inclusive economies\nFunding\nGrants and awards\nApplying for funding\nManaging funds\nResources for IDRC grantees\nPartnerships\nAbout IDRC\nAbout\nCareers\nAnnual review\nTransparency\nLeadership\nPolicies and commitments\nNews and events\nNews\nEvents\nPerspectives\nResearch in Action\nStories\nMedia\nFulltext search\nHome\nFunding\nConnecting Indigenous Research Leadership in Canada and the Global South\nClosed\nCall for\nProposals\nDeadline\nTuesday, September 23, 2025 - 23:59 ET\nPrograms\nEducation and Science\nDuration\n12 months\nFunded by\nIDRC\nBudget\nCAD 700,000\nPoint of contact\neducationandscience@idrc.ca\nType\nGrant\nStatus\nClosed\nScope\nIDRC is pleased to announce a call for proposals to connect Indigenous research and leadership in Canada and in the Global South to complement the Tri-agency strategic funding opportunity\nIndigenous Capacity and Leadership in Research Connection Grants\nbeing led by the Social Sciences and Humanities Research Council (SSHRC).\nThis call is open to Indigenous organizations or organizations supporting Indigenous-led research programs based in the Global South. If you are an organization based in Canada, please consult the\nTri-agency strategic funding\n.\nThe call expects to fund up to seven grants for Indigenous organizations in the Global South that are interested in connecting with First Nations, Métis and Inuit communities in Canada through knowledge-sharing activities. These activities aim to co-develop an interdisciplinary, Indigenous research agenda and build alliances between Indigenous researchers in the Global South and First Nations, Métis and Inuit researchers in Canada, potentially leading to broader joint research endeavors in the future.\nIDRC will allocate up to CAD700,000 through this call, with projects receiving up to CAD100,000 each. Each individual project will be 12 months in duration.\nEligibility\nTo be eligible, the Lead Applicant Organization must be a legally recognized, not-for-profit research-focused entity headquartered in an eligible country within the region of operation and must be Indigenous or support Indigenous-led research programs involving Indigenous researchers, particularly women or gender-diverse individuals.\nGovernment bodies, individuals and branches of international organizations are not eligible to apply.\nMore details\nFor more information, please read the\ndetailed call for proposals document\nand the\nFrequently Asked Questions\n.\nMore questions? Please direct them to\neducationandscience@idrc.ca\n.\nReady to apply?\nTo apply for this funding opportunity, you’ll need an account on SurveyMonkey Apply. If you don’t have an account yet, or need help with your existing one, please refer to our\nAccount setup guide\n.\nGet started\nShare this page\nStay connected.\nSubscribe\nIDRC / Eduardo Jalil, Panos Pictures\nFooter\nCareers\nContact Us\nDigital library\nMedia\nSub Footer Menu\nAccessibility\nEquality Stateme",
