    "description": "Funding opportunities - Research Council of Finland\nTo main content\nAbout the RCF\nAbout us\nRCF at a glance\nStrategy\nSustainable development\nAcademicians of Science\nRCF Awards\nWorking at the RCF\nContact us\nRCF organisation\nOrganisation\nManagement\nDecision-making bodies\nWhat's new\nPress releases and news\nOpinions\nNewsletter\nBlog\nEvents\nMedia services\nResearch funding\nFunding opportunities\nSpark funding\nAcademy Project Funding\nAcademy Research Fellowship\nAcademy Professorship\nClinical Researcher Funding\nForge funding\nFinnish Flagships\nResearch infrastructures\nFinnish Centres of Excellence\nInternational collaboration in high-performance computing\nShift funding\nProof of Concept Funding\nFunding for clinical research\nFunding for university research profiles\nInternational funding cooperation\nFunding from EU Recovery and Resilience Facility (RRF)\nSport Science and Physical Activity – ACTIVE\nStrategic research funding\nApply for funding\nCalls for applications\nA–Z index of application guidelines\nAsk & Apply\nHow to use funding\nReport on your project\nReview and funding decisions\nHow applications are reviewed\nReview and decision-making\nGuidelines and forms for reviewers\nHow decisions are made\nFunding decisions\nResponsible Science\nFrom research to society\nResearch impact\nNew knowledge\nExpertise and experts\nInnovations for business and society\nRCF impact\nData dashboards\nPublications\nInternational cooperation\nOpinions\nEvents\nResponsible science\nResponsible research funding\nGood scientific practice and research ethics\nResearch security\nEquality and nondiscrimination\nOpen science\nSustainable development\nResponsible researcher evaluation\nOnline services\nFI\nSV\nFI\nSV\nOnline services\nFunding opportunities\nThe RCF’s funding portfolio can be divided into three categories, each with specific impact objectives.\nSpark – Novel and bold research ideas with long-term focus\nThe aim of the RCF funding category Spark is to ensure a high-quality scientific foundation for the Finnish research and innovation system now and in the future.\nSpark funding identifies researcher-driven bold research ideas and advances innovative, broad-based research in the long term.\nForge – Cutting-edge expertise for society’s benefit\nThe aim of the RCF funding category Forge is to pool together the best experts, ideas and tools. Forge funding strengthens existing and creates new internationally attractive research environments for scientific excellence that produce knowledge and expertise for use in society.\nShift – Solving societal challenges together\nShift is a funding category comprising RCF funding and funding provided by the Strategic Research Council. It seeks to solve societal challenges and promote the versatile use of research knowledge to benefit Finland and the world.\nShift funding strengthens the societal impact of research by increasing interaction between knowledge producers and users and research and innovation funders.\nDo you have questions or feedback for us?\nContact us\nResearch Council of Finland\nHakaniemenranta 6\nPO Box 131\nFI-00531 Helsinki\nSwitchboard: +358 295 335 000\nRegistry: +358 295 335 100\nEmail: kirjaamo@aka.fi\nContact us\nInvoicing\nSubscribe to our newsletter\nData protection\nAccessibility statement\nAccessibility feedback\nWhistleblower protection\nDocument publicity\nCookie policy",
