    "objective": "to address conceptual and technical barriers to improve understanding of how changes in the molecular networks surrounding cells leads to tissue decline. This has the potential to positively impact chronic diseases including cancer and fibrosis",
    "description": "Major initiatives and directed funding – Research funding | Wellcome\nSkip to main content\nThis website will not work correctly in Internet Explorer 11 and it is strongly recommended that you upgrade to an up-to-date browser. Internet Explorer 11 will go out of support and be retired on June 15, 2022. For more information on upgrading please see\nbrowser-update.org\n.\nLooking for Wellcome Collection?\nClose\nLooking for Wellcome Collection? banner\nWellcome home\nSearch\nMenu\nClose\nHome\nResearch funding\nResearch funding\nWe fund research around the world, across a broad range of disciplines, to understand life, health and wellbeing and to deliver equitable health solutions.\nResearch funding overview\nFind a funding opportunity\nFunding guidance\nPrepare to apply\nFunding policies and grant conditions\nOur funding portfolio\nFunded grants\nMajor initiatives\nLogin to Wellcome Funding\nEngagement and advocacy\nEngagement and advocacy\nWe work with communities, governments and partners across the world to advocate for evidence-based health policies that support the communities most affected.\nEngagement and advocacy overview\nEngaging people\nWellcome Collection\nWellcome Global Monitor\nAdvocacy and partnerships\nScience Policy Labs\nOur priorities\nOur priorities\nWe're bringing together expertise from across science, innovation and society to generate new knowledge and find equitable solutions to improve life, health and wellbeing.\nOur priorities overview\nClimate and Health\nInfectious Disease\nMental Health\nDiscovery Research\nOur strategy\nEquity\nSustainability\nInsights and impact\nInsights and impact\nRead our insights to learn more about our activities and impact supporting our mission.\nExplore insights\nExplore our impact\nArticles\nReports\nPodcast\nNewsletters\nAbout us\nAbout us\nWe are a charitable foundation with a vision of a healthier future for everyone.\nAbout us overview\nOur people\nOur governance\nOur teams\nWork with us\nJobs\nContract opportunities\nOur history\nHow we are funded\nMedia queries\nContact us\nSearch\nBack to menu\nResearch funding\nWe fund research around the world, across a broad range of disciplines, to understand life, health and wellbeing and to deliver equitable health solutions.\nResearch funding overview\nFind a funding opportunity\nFunding guidance\nPrepare to apply\nFunding policies and grant conditions\nOur funding portfolio\nFunded grants\nMajor initiatives\nLogin to Wellcome Funding\nBack to menu\nEngagement and advocacy\nWe work with communities, governments and partners across the world to advocate for evidence-based health policies that support the communities most affected.\nEngagement and advocacy overview\nEngaging people\nWellcome Collection\nWellcome Global Monitor\nAdvocacy and partnerships\nScience Policy Labs\nBack to menu\nOur priorities\nWe're bringing together expertise from across science, innovation and society to generate new knowledge and find equitable solutions to improve life, health and wellbeing.\nOur priorities overview\nClimate and Health\nInfectious Disease\nMental Health\nDiscovery Research\nOur strategy\nEquity\nSustainability\nBack to menu\nInsights and impact\nRead our insights to learn more about our activities and impact supporting our mission.\nExplore insights\nExplore our impact\nArticles\nReports\nPodcast\nNewsletters\nBack to menu\nAbout us\nWe are a charitable foundation with a vision of a healthier future for everyone.\nAbout us overview\nOur people\nOur governance\nOur teams\nWork with us\nJobs\nContract opportunities\nOur history\nHow we are funded\nMedia queries\nContact us\nClose\nsearch\nSearch\nSearch\nHide Search\nClose search and menu\nMajor initiatives and directed funding\nTackling some of the biggest challenges in research requires a long-term perspective and a sizeable focus. We call this area of work our directed funding.\nOur support and contributions to these initiatives are designed to give glob