n help you find experts to interview, provide ideas on articles about science and research, and provide photos and other materials.\nLooking for information on RCF-funded research and researchers?\nFunding granted by the Research Council of Finland (research.fi)\nResearch.fi is a service offered by the Finnish Ministry of Education, Science and Culture that collects and shares information on research and researchers in Finland. The service contains information on scientific publications by Finnish organisations, projects funded by public and private research funders, researchers in Finland and their research activities, and statistical information on research personnel, research funding and the impact of scientific publications.\nThe service is based on a national research information hub, which pools data maintained by universities, universities of applied sciences, research institutes and research funders in their own services.\nLooking for information on impact of RCF-funded research?\nLearn more on our website\nResearch impact\nOur impact site provides a wide variety of information on the impact of scientific research and research funding.\nData dashboards\nThe RCF dashboards provide key data on research funding granted by the RCF and the Strategic Research Council (SRC).\nPress releases\nSubscribe to our press releases via\nSTT Info\n. The service allows you to read our news releases and other RCF publications. All material published in the service is freely available to the media.\nOur experts\nGet in touch.\nOur email addresses are in the format firstname.lastname(at)aka.fi.\nCommunications and public relations\nIn RCF-related media inquiries or inquiries concerning the RCF management team, please contact\nRiitta Tirronen\n, Senior Communications Specialist, tel. +358 295 335 118 or Communications Specialists\nPekka Rautio\n(tel. +358 295 335 040),\nVesa Varpula\n(tel. +358 295 335 131) or\nAnna Oravakangas\n(tel. +358 295 335 039).\nYou can also reach us by 