    "description": "Women’s Voice and Leadership Learning Partnership: Regional Learning Hubs | IDRC - International Development Research Centre\nSkip to main content\nTo homepage\nTo homepage\nEnglish\nFrançais\nEspañol\nToggle Menu\nToggle Menu\nFulltext search\nMobile Main Navigation\nWhat we do\nWhere we work\nHow we work\nProjects we support\nClimate resilient food systems\nGlobal health\nEducation and science\nDemocratic and inclusive governance\nSustainable inclusive economies\nFunding\nGrants and awards\nApplying for funding\nManaging funds\nResources for IDRC grantees\nPartnerships\nAbout IDRC\nAbout\nCareers\nAnnual review\nTransparency\nLeadership\nPolicies and commitments\nNews and events\nNews\nEvents\nPerspectives\nResearch in Action\nStories\nMedia\nTo homepage\nEnglish\nFrançais\nEspañol\nToggle Menu\nFooter\nCareers\nContact Us\nDigital library\nSub Footer Menu\nAccessibility\nEquality Statement\nOpen access policy\nPrivacy Notice\nResearch ethics\nTerms of use\nTransparency\nMain navigation\nWhat we do\nWhere we work\nHow we work\nProjects we support\nClimate resilient food systems\nGlobal health\nEducation and science\nDemocratic and inclusive governance\nSustainable inclusive economies\nFunding\nGrants and awards\nApplying for funding\nManaging funds\nResources for IDRC grantees\nPartnerships\nAbout IDRC\nAbout\nCareers\nAnnual review\nTransparency\nLeadership\nPolicies and commitments\nNews and events\nNews\nEvents\nPerspectives\nResearch in Action\nStories\nMedia\nFulltext search\nHome\nFunding\nWomen’s Voice and Leadership Learning Partnership: Regional Learning Hubs\nClosed\nCall for\nProposals\nDeadline\nSunday, November 30, 2025 - 23:59 ET\nPrograms\nDemocratic and Inclusive Governance\nWomen’s Voice and Leadership Learning Partnership\nDuration\n42 Months\nTopic(s)\nGender\nFunded by\nGlobal Affairs Canada and IDRC\nBudget\nAmounts to vary by regions – refer to the detailed call for proposals\nPoint of contact\nLP-PA@idrc.ca\nType\nGrant\nStatus\nClosed\nScope\nGlobal Affairs Canada and IDRC are supporting a\nLearning Partnership\nto enhance the efforts and impacts of the flagship program, Women’s Voice and Leadership, renewed in 2023. This call for proposals seeks to recruit four organizations (or consortia of organizations) for the Learning Partnership’s Regional Learning Hubs.\nThe hubs will support localized learning, evidence generation and knowledge sharing among women’s rights organizations, LGBTQI+ groups and their networks. They will complement the Global Learning Hub by anchoring learning activities in regional contexts and ensuring that insights are grounded in local realities.\nEach hub will co-lead a participatory process to contextualize the co-created learning agenda. This includes overseeing region-specific learning priorities, questions and approaches that reflect the lived experiences and advocacy strategies of local actors. Each hub will also be responsible for organizing region-specific convenings and virtual engagements, fostering vibrant learning ecosystems that strengthen advocacy and interventions to advance gender equality.\nEligibility\nThis call for proposals is intended for women’s rights and feminist organizations or consortia of such organizations that are primarily governed, led, and based in the Global South. Organizations from the Global North are also eligible if they primarily operate in countries that receive Official Development Assistance and have as their core mission the promotion of the rights of women, youth, girls, and gender-diverse people.\nApplicants will need to demonstrate previous experience in applying feminist monitoring, evaluation and learning practices, with an interest in demonstrating the benefits of feminist or gender-transformative approaches, and be able to perform services in English, French and Spanish, at a minimum.\nMore details\nFor more information, please consult the\ndetailed call for proposals\n.\nLearn more about the\nLearning Partnership\n.\nBefore starting your application on the Survey Monkey Apply platform, please review\nthis application form\nto see the full list of question",
