 premier expert in science policy and a key developer of international research collaboration in Finland. We owe our success to a wide array of experts who possess both ambition and drive.\nThe core values guiding our activities are openness, transparency, reliability, equality and nondiscrimination. Accountability is a key principle for us and for all research we fund.\nWe want to ensure the competence and wellbeing of our employees and help them enjoy their work. We offer excellent opportunities for professional development and skills training. An ongoing commitment to improving staff skills and wellbeing supports our self-renewal and our responsible and interactive engagement with the scientific community and the wider society.\nIn the workplace, we are inspired and we grow and develop collectively.\nWe work together, continue to learn and boldly try out new ideas.\nWe maintain a positive atmosphere in the workplace and support each other’s wellbeing.\nWe continue to develop the diversity of our workplace.\nWe are committed to the principles of a safer space. A safer space refers to a culture of discussion where diversity is valued and discrimination is not tolerated. A safer workplace creates a work community where everyone has the opportunity to be themselves and feel that they belong.\nMore information\nOrganisation\nHow we promote equality and nondiscrimination\nRCF vacancies are announced in the Government online recruitment system at\nwww.valtiolle.fi\n.\nFollow us on LinkedIn\n.\nPrint page\nStaff\n110\nWomen\n66%\nMen\n34%\nAverage age\n52.3\nMaster's degree\n84%\nDoctoral degree\n47%\nJob satisfaction (1–4)\n3.17\nShare page\nStaff\n110\nWomen\n66%\nMen\n34%\nAverage age\n52.3\nMaster's degree\n84%\nDoctoral degree\n47%\nJob satisfaction (1–4)\n3.17\nShare page\nDo you have questions or feedback for us?\nContact us\nResearch Council of Finland\nHakaniemenranta 6\nPO Box 131\nFI-00531 Helsinki\nSwitchboard: +358 295 335 000\nRegistry: +358 295 335 100\nEm